## The data is not under this licence, and that distinction is deliberate

The MIT terms above cover the **code** in this repository: `src/`, `scripts/`, `tests/`,
`app/`, `sql/`, the `Makefile`, the `Dockerfile`, and the documentation.

The **redistributed data** carries its own licence and its own obligations:

- `data/snapshot.parquet` and every file derived from it
- the figures and reports computed from it under `reports/` and `docs/`

> **Data: ENTSO-E Transparency Platform; Bundesnetzagentur | SMARD.de — CC BY 4.0.**

Both sources publish under Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). Redistribution is permitted **with
attribution**, which is why the line above appears on every public surface of this
project rather than only here.

This split was a design constraint from the start, not an afterthought. The project's
own scope record (`capstone_V6_8.md` §0 item 3) closes a gas-price feature on exactly
this ground: no free, daily, **legally redistributable** TTF/THE series exists — Yahoo's
terms prohibit redistribution and Ember's underlying series is licensed — so the feature
was omitted rather than built on data that could not be committed to a public repository.
A reproducible open repository that cannot legally ship its own inputs is not
reproducible.

## The trained model

`models/champion/` is a derived work of the CC BY 4.0 data above. It is released under the
MIT terms in this file, with the data attribution carried alongside it — in
`models/champion/champion_card.json`, on the registered `champion` alias, and on every
public surface.
